{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain for about six days and haven’t been able to keep food down for three days. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been really bad. The pain is constant, and I keep throwing up. I tried to eat a little, but it just comes back up. My stomach feels full all the time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You have type 1 diabetes and gastroparesis, so this could be related to poor blood sugar control or a flare of your chronic condition. Your blood sugar was very high when you arrived—527. We gave you some insulin, and it’s now down to 228."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I couldn’t eat, so I wasn’t sure how much insulin to take. I didn’t want to go too low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. We’re giving you 80% of your usual long-acting insulin dose since you’re not eating. We’ll keep monitoring your sugars. We also noticed your sodium was low—132—which likely improved with fluids. It’s probably from the vomiting or a condition called SIADH."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had low sodium before. Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be if it drops too fast, but yours was mild and is already improving. You’re drinking now, and your exam shows you’re not dehydrated, so we’re not worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. My pain is still really bad. Can I get something stronger?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2158-02-04 22:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve given you IV hydromorphone, and you can have it every three hours as needed. We’re also watching for signs of pancreatitis, but your lipase is normal, so it’s likely your usual gastroparesis flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2158-02-04 23:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why did you use my GJ tube for meds? I didn’t want that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2158-02-04 23:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We used it to give you medications since you couldn’t swallow, but I understand you’re upset. We should have discussed it with you first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2158-02-04 23:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I pulled it out. I don’t want it anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2158-02-04 23:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. We’ve consulted your primary care doctor and psychiatric services. Since you’re not in immediate danger and you’re making this decision voluntarily, we won’t replace it. But you’ll need to care for the site to prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar was 414 this morning, but no ketones in your urine, so it’s not DKA. Your anion gap was slightly elevated but has resolved. We’ll send you home on your usual insulin doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t feel safe going home. My roommate has been sexually assaulting me. I’m scared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry you’re going through that. You mentioned earlier you had thoughts of hurting him. Is that still how you feel?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m angry. But I won’t do anything. I just don’t want to go back there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve spoken with a psychiatric nurse who’s supporting you. You’re alert and coherent, and you’re not suicidal. You said you have other places to go—can you stay there safely?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I can stay with a friend. I just need my meds and my things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ll discharge you home with your usual medications. No changes have been made. You’ll need to keep the GJ tube site clean and dry. Follow up with your primary doctor soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I get another GJ tube somewhere else?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s something to discuss with another provider. We’re not replacing it here, but you’re free to seek care elsewhere if you choose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain meds? I still need them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll go home with your usual hydromorphone, gabapentin, and other medications. Use them as prescribed. If pain worsens, please reach out to your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my asthma? I haven’t used my inhalers much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lungs sound clear, and your oxygen levels are normal. Keep using your Advair and albuterol as needed. No changes there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I think I’m ready to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2158-02-05 06:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care of yourself, and please follow up with your primary care provider. If anything changes, don’t hesitate to come back."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2158-02-04 22:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2158-02-05 14:49:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with a six-day history of nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain, unable to tolerate oral intake for three days. She has type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, chronic pain, and borderline personality disorder. On admission, she had severe hyperglycemia (glucose 527) and hyponatremia (Na 132), both of which improved with IV insulin and fluids. Her anion gap metabolic acidosis resolved without progression to DKA. During the admission, she removed her GJ tube in protest over staff using it for medications, and after consultation, it was not replaced. She expressed homicidal ideation toward her roommate, whom she accused of sexual assault, but remained coherent and alert, opting to stay with a friend. She tolerated oral intake by morning and was discharged home on her prior medication regimen with wound care instructions for the GJ site.",
    "problems": [
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Acidosis",
      "Other acute pain",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
